LangGraph helps to build workflows for LLM applications
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Why not just use LangChain?

This is an important question.

Think of it like this:

LangChain gives you components:

LLM
Tools
Retriever
Prompt
Chains

LangGraph lets you connect those components into a controlled workflow:

         ┌── Tool 1 ──┐
         │            │
LLM ─────┼── Tool 2 ──┼── LLM ── Answer
         │            │
         └── RAG ─────┘


LangChain gives you the building blocks.

LangGraph lets you connect those blocks into a stateful workflow/agent with branching and loops.



